{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And Elohim said to Noah, 'The end of all flesh'</b> A hint to the days of the Flood, which are like the numerical value of קץ — 40 days of rain and 150 of intensification." "<b>For the earth is filled with violence through them</b> In gematria: גלוי עריות (uncovering of nakedness / sexual immorality)." "<b>והנני</b> Three times in the Masorah: והנני משחיתם, והנני אומר לבנות בית בשילה, והנני מקוששת שנים עצים. Said HaShem: I said to build, that the world should be built, and they corrupted their deeds. והנני משחיתם and והנני מקוששת — to teach you that no tree remained standing; all were uprooted." "<b>משחיתם</b> In gematria: היא שלשה טפחים." "<b>משחיתם את הארץ</b> Rashei tevot: מאה. Teaches you that He destroyed their stature, which was one hundred cubits high."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {2 "The juxtaposition of 'והנני משחיתם' with 'והנני מקוששת' (a woman gathering wood, 2 Kings 6:2 context for Shiloh is actually Jeremiah 7:14 'והנני אומר לבנות בית בשילה') is read as: the destruction uprooted all trees, so she 'gathers' wood because none stand."}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:15:47.427506897Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}